  {
   "id": 366672,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "In a house, a single incoming wire at a high potential with respect to the ground provides electric power. How are the appliances connected between this wire and the ground, in parallel or in series? Explain.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 888981,
     "content_html": "The appliances are connected in parallel to provide different voltage differences across each appliance."
    },
    {
     "id": 888982,
     "content_html": "The appliances are connected in parallel to provide the same voltage difference across each appliance."
    },
    {
     "id": 888983,
     "content_html": "The appliances are connected in series to provide the same voltage difference across each appliance."
    },
    {
     "id": 888984,
     "content_html": "The appliances are connected in series to provide different voltage differences across each appliance."
    }
